      sources: "Sources: Chapter 13, “The code: what examples/non-person-identity adds”; the validation kit's check (WD-172); “What it never does.”",
      say: `So what does the code add? One script and one module, running one read-only task. A config file declares the export commands an operator runs, every one a generate, get or list, and the module runs none of them. A test fails if the code ever calls the AWS or O C I command line, or makes a web request. Every run writes a folder: findings, identities, trust, a credentials list with identifiers only, never a secret, the evidence rows, and a manifest with each input's hash and any optional file it couldn't read. The validation kit's check, V K N P I ten, reads the same folder for the guide's gates; this kit gives the full findings behind it. And it changes nothing: the findings say what to do, and a person does it.`,
      detail: `Invoke-NpiCloudWorkload.ps1 and the module powershell/NpiCloudWorkload add one read-only task, cloud-workload. config/calls-ch13.json declares the export commands an operator runs, every one a generate, get or list; the module runs none of them, and a test fails if its code ever calls aws or oci or makes a web request. Its controls and KSIs per step are in config/requirements-ch13.json. Every run writes a folder with findings.json, identities.json, credentials.csv (identifiers only, never a secret), trust.json, evidence.json and a manifest.json with each input's SHA-256, the export commands the inputs came from and any optional file not read. The same inputs and -AsOf date give byte-identical files. The validation kit's check: the guide's G1 and G3 gates name VK-NPI-10 (WD-172), which reads the same export folder in examples/validation-kit and reports the gate's pass criteria: long-lived credentials without a current exception, missing tags, OIDC trusts without a sub condition and trust anchors without an imported CRL. This chapter's kit gives the full findings behind it. What it never does: it runs no AWS or OCI command and calls no API. It deactivates no key, deletes no identity and changes no policy. The guide's orphan rule disables first and a person acts; the findings say what to do, and a person does it.`,
