      part: "What", title: "Not yet specified: six open questions",
      body: [
        { table: { head: ["Open question", "What the pages read say", "What the kit does"], w: [3.3, 5.05, 3.8], rows: [
          ["AWS GovCloud (US) and Entra, either way", "Outbound federation across AWS partitions is documented, not to an outside relying party such as Entra; no page walks through Entra federating into GovCloud", "Only reports OIDC trusts; the guide uses either path only after a test (WD-171)"],
          ["IAM Access Analyzer's unused-access findings in GovCloud", "Policy generation isn't available; no other gap named", "NPI-AWS-03 doesn't depend on it"],
          ["Instance principals, resource principals and OKE workload identity in OC2", "Oracle's OC2 page doesn't address them", "Confirm them for the program's tenancy"],
          ["The OCI CLI's output field names", "Not shown on the CLI reference pages", "Reads any spelling; Lab 2, step 4 records what the CLI prints"],
          ["Which credential report column is which key", "The report names no key ID", "Joins by creation date; no match: “last used unknown”"],
          ["Users in an identity domain", "Whether user list returns every domain's users isn't stated; domains apply to OC2 tenancies created after Jan 17, 2023", "Open"],
        ] }, pt: 11.5 },
        { lead: "These are open, and the kit doesn't assume an answer." },
      ],
      sources: "Sources: AWS, GovCloud IAM. Oracle, Oracle US Government Cloud. Learn, workload identity federation. Decision register, WD-171. Chapter 13, “Verified facts” — not yet specified.",
      say: `Six things are still open, and the kit doesn't assume an answer to any of them. First, AWS GovCloud and Entra, in either direction. AWS documents GovCloud's outbound federation across its own partitions, but no page read walks through Entra and GovCloud trusting each other, so the guide uses either path only after a test. Second, whether Access Analyzer's unused-access findings run in GovCloud; the kit's ninety-day check doesn't depend on it. Third, whether instance principals, resource principals and O K E workload identity are available in O C two. Fourth, the O C I command line's output field names. Fifth, which credential report column belongs to which key. And sixth, whether the O C I user list returns users in every identity domain.`,
      detail: `Not yet specified; open, and the kit doesn't assume an answer. AWS GovCloud (US) and Entra, either way: AWS documents GovCloud for outbound federation across AWS partitions, not to an outside relying party such as Entra; no page read walks through a customer Entra tenant federating into a GovCloud account. The guide uses either path only after a test (WD-171). IAM Access Analyzer's unused-access findings in GovCloud: the GovCloud IAM page says policy generation isn't available and names no other gap; whether unused-access findings run there isn't stated. The kit's NPI-AWS-03 doesn't depend on it. Instance principals, resource principals and OKE workload identity in OC2: Oracle's OC2 page doesn't address them. Confirm them for the program's tenancy. The OCI CLI's output field names: not shown on the CLI reference pages; the kit reads any spelling, and Lab 2, step 4 records what the CLI prints. Which credential report column is which key: the report names no key ID; the kit joins by creation date. A key with no matching column gets "last used unknown". Users in an identity domain: whether oci iam user list returns every identity domain's users in a tenancy that has identity domains isn't stated on the page read; identity domains apply to OC2 tenancies created after January 17, 2023.`,
