      say: `Here's what done looks like. The guide's exports, tags and CRLs included, run in every GovCloud account, and in the tenancy's home region. Every role, workload user, O C I user with a credential, and dynamic group carries a system I D, two owners and a sponsor, or is in an orphan ticket. Every long-lived credential has an exception with a replacement date, or a ticket to replace it. No O C I key is older than ninety days, and no root access key is active. Every O I D C trust names its workload, and every outside or open principal is removed or justified. Every trust anchor has an imported CRL. No dynamic group reaches the whole tenancy without a reason. And each run's evidence and manifest are filed with the change record.`,
      detail: `Checklist: the guide's Step 1g exports, its tag and CRL reads included, run in every AWS GovCloud (US) account; Step 1h runs in the tenancy's home region. Every role, workload IAM user, OCI user holding a credential and dynamic group carries SystemId, two owners and a sponsor, or is in an orphan ticket (NPI-AWS-08, NPI-OCI-06). Every active long-lived credential has an exception with a replacement date in the exception register, or a ticket to replace it (NPI-AWS-01, -05; NPI-OCI-01, -04, -05). No OCI API key is older than 90 days (NPI-OCI-02), and no user holds a second active key or access key outside a rotation (NPI-AWS-02, NPI-OCI-03). No root user access key is active (NPI-AWS-07). Every OIDC trust names its workload in a sub condition (NPI-AWS-09); every outside account, * and other-partition principal is removed or justified (NPI-AWS-11 to -13). Every enabled Roles Anywhere trust anchor has an imported CRL, refreshed on the certificate calendar (NPI-AWS-14). No dynamic group matches the whole tenancy or holds manage all-resources without a recorded reason (NPI-OCI-08, -09). Each run's evidence.json and manifest.json are filed with the change record. Continue the book: previous, Chapter 12, The Managed Service Account Standard; the workbook index; the implementation guide's AWS and OCI steps.`,
